  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual claim of universal fear",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'every one is afraid of this man', which implicitly positions the viewer as part of the collective 'everyone' who is afraid. This creates a semiotic projection where the user identifies with the group experiencing fear toward the depicted figure, thereby internalizing the meme's hateful framing. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the universal quantifier 'every one' functions as an implicit projection of the user into the collective subject of fear.",
